course: dictionary
lesson: 818
title: Belief: what you hold to be true
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A belief is something you think is true. You may feel sure of it, but you cannot always prove it. «A belief that ghosts exist» is still a belief, because someone holds it, even though nobody has tested it.
explain: Belief can also mean trust in someone. «Her belief in me helped me win» means she trusted me and was confident I could do it. «Self-belief» means believing in yourself, and «beyond belief» means so amazing or shocking that you can hardly believe it.
explain: A belief can be a religious or moral idea that a person holds. «Religious beliefs» are the ideas a faith holds to be true. People have different beliefs, and you can respect someone's belief even if you do not share it.
fact: A belief is something you think is true, even if you cannot prove it.
fact: Belief can mean trust: «belief in someone» means confidence in them.
fact: «Beyond belief» means amazing or shocking.
fact: «Religious beliefs» are the ideas a faith holds to be true.
fact: «You do not have to share a belief to be respectful about it.»
exercise: «A belief that ghosts exist» is an example of what? | A shopping list | *A belief, something thought to be true without proof | A sport | A fact, proved by a test in a lab
exercise: «Her belief in me helped me win.» In this sentence, belief means what? | *Trust and confidence in someone | Being very tired | A religious idea | A map of the town
exercise: Which phrase means so amazing you can hardly believe it? | *beyond belief | self-belief | belief in | religious beliefs
test: Why do we respect other people's beliefs, even when we disagree with them? | Because beliefs are always wrong | Because we must always change our belief to match theirs | *Because we can respect a belief without sharing it | Because everyone is entitled to hold their own beliefs, and we can discuss them politely
test: Which word means trust and confidence in yourself? | *self-belief | evidence | beyond belief | fact
exam: Which sentence uses belief to mean a religious or moral idea? | «Her belief in me helped me win.» | *«Churches differ in leaders and worship, but all share belief in one God.» | «It was beyond belief how fast he ran.» | «She has self-belief in her own talent.»
